 "stimulus_html": "Compute the probabilities (rounded to 3 decimal places) of the following events related to rolling a standard 4-sided die (with faces labeled 1, 2, 3, and 4):",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 516835,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You roll the die 10 times and get exactly four 2s.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Binomial formula: For a binomial experiment with <i>n</i> trials and <i>p</i> probability of success in each trial, then P(number of <i>a</i> successes) = <span data-math=\"nCa \\times {p^a} \\times {\\left( {1 - p} \\right)^{n - a}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>There is one 2 out of 4 sides, so <i>p</i> is <span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{4}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>P(exactly four 2s in 10 rolls) =<span data-math=\"\\left( {10C4} \\right){\\left( {\\frac{1}{4}} \\right)^4}{\\left( {1 - \\frac{1}{4}} \\right)^{10 - 4}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {210} \\right){\\left( {\\frac{1}{4}} \\right)^4}{\\left( {\\frac{3}{4}} \\right)^6} = \\frac{{153,090}}{{1,048,576}} \\approx 0.146\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.146"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
